// Realtime Database rules for Prajadhwani.
//
// Deny-by-default. The RTDB instance is enabled and ready, but no feature
// reads or writes it yet — all app data lives in Firestore, which has its
// own rules in firestore.rules. An enabled database with permissive rules
// and no owner is exactly how civic apps leak data, so this stays shut
// until something actually needs it.
//
// To use it, add a named path with its own rules rather than loosening
// these — e.g. a /presence/$uid node writable only by that uid. Never put
// anything here that identifies a reporter: the whole privacy model is
// that officials see a token number, a problem and an area, never a person
// (see functions/src/public/onSubmissionWritten.ts).
{
  "rules": {
    ".read": false,
    ".write": false
  }
}
